{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1546326-few-rules-questions","id":1546326,"title":"Few rules questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-23T19:50:54-08:00","id":1546326,"title":"Few rules questions","content":"Is it stated anywhere if there's a maximum for attributes and skills? I'm assuming 5 dots, but it doesn't actually seem to say anywhere. Does that mean there isn't a maximum, or they forgot to put that in the book?<br /> <br /> Field Medic says if you are close enough to provide aid, you can administer First Aid in one round. What does that mean exactly? When does the First Aid actually happen? Is it automatic or do you still have to roll? If the last bit is just saying you can make a normal first aid roll on your next turn, then is the only real benefit from the Edge the ability to spend a momentum to move towards a damaged ally? Also, since first aid isn't how you heal injury levels, why would Field Medic trigger when an ally is damaged? Shouldn't it trigger when an ally takes a negative condition that can be treated with first aid?<br /> <br /> If someone is suffering from multiple physical conditions, do you need a separate First Aid roll to heal each condition, or is it 1 hit per condition ended, so a good enough roll can end all the conditions at once?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-24T06:53:53-08:00","id":1546336,"title":"","content":"So I think you're right that the rulebook currently does not state that either Attributes or Skills have a maximum value, at least not anywhere I can see. I <b>think</b> the errata form has closed now but obviously this needs to be in the game.<br /> <br /> As for first aid: currently it seems like First Aid isn't actually a game mechanically defined concept. It's mentioned in the resolution text for various Status Effects but that's mostly reserved for in world text, there's no particular indication that &quot;first aid&quot; is a mechanical term any more than, say &quot;restore reputation&quot;.<br /> <br /> I suspect that the game assumes the once per scene Healing Roll you're allowed to make constitutes &quot;First Aid&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":". 11-24-2024, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-24T07:38:54-08:00","id":1546338,"title":"","content":"1) Huh... I checked Skills and Attributes, and searched the whole manuscript for &quot;dot,&quot; &quot;rate,&quot; &quot;rating,&quot; &quot;maximum,&quot; and it does not specify a maximum anywhere - and the Entanglement table only covers maximum curse dice and what foundation spells you can learn. I would <i>presume</i> the maximum is supposed to be 5 in each trait, but the rules do not actually say that.<br /> <br /> 2&amp;3) Healing (under Damage) describes removing both damage and status effects as an Intellect + Medicine action, maximum once per scene per patient (not provider), treating the highest &quot;level&quot; of injury as the difficulty, and any status effects the character possesses can be bought off as if they were complications. The Edge states that once you move close enough, you administer &quot;First Aid&quot; (capitalized with a p.XX reference) in one round. Multiple status effects resolve immediately when the character receives first aid, and presumably do not need to be bought off as other physical ailments might - unfortunately, a &quot;First Aid&quot; action to correspond to the page reference is not described anywhere in the manuscript other than the Cunning + Medicine entry under Medicine's description. Medicine also describes the rolled Attribute changing to Composure if you're operating on yourself - from this, I would guess that the intention is that the once-per-scene healing's rolled Attribute changes by setting (with the caveat that first aid can only be applied once, and further healing must be Intellect-based), and Field Medic allows you to rush the first aid version of once-per-scene healing as a single mid-combat action instead of having to wait until combat ends to have sufficient time for it.<br /> <br /> As to why the movement is triggered by damage, not by a status effect? Likely because aside from Aggravated Wound (which instead marks a specific injury level itself), most status effects that would be affected by first aid will be riding the coattails of an injury anyway, while there are &quot;Combat&quot; status effects like Grappled that first aid should have no effect on, so they can't just say &quot;when a negative status effect is inflicted&quot; - they would have to list all the relevant status effects individually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3388-r0gue_rob0t","name":"r0gue_rob0t","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-24T17:06:06-08:00","id":1546357,"title":"","content":"Another quick question, sorry, I'm probably going to have a bunch of these. There are several tricks, like trip and disarm for melee attacks, which seem to just allow you to do things to an enemy. Does the enemy not get any chance to resist these tricks? You'd think it would be harder to disarm someone who is stronger and/or more skilled than you. Unless I've missed something it looks like you just pay the hits and the trick just happens. Is that really how it's meant to work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-24T17:56:15-08:00","id":1546358,"title":"","content":"That one fortunately has a very simple answer - they already failed their chance to resist when they allowed you to generate enough hits over their Defense to buy any Tricks at all.<br /> <br /> The actual probability of generating 4+ hits (assuming double 10s, no Enhancement, and Defense 2 for a moment) is really low - we're talking around 24% at 6 dice, and not reaching even as good as a coin toss until 10 dice. Even with a +1 Enhancement for a weapon, that only improves to about 44% at 6 dice, needing 7 dice to reach a coin toss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3388-r0gue_rob0t","name":"r0gue_rob0t","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-24T18:25:07-08:00","id":1546360,"title":"","content":"As r0gue_rob0t points out, it's taken into account by the higher Defence of stronger enemies. Plus you'll often also be wanting to buy off Complications from Area Effects or Dread Powers.<br /> <br /> I also don't think Trip does as much as it seems, it's always possible to combine actions so if you trip an opponent then back away they can still make a combined action to stand up and approach (there's no rule saying this is allowed but it's an application of the general rule for combining actions). Disarm is better but it only works on non-worn non-natural weapons.<br /> <br /> Also the GM is well within their rights to rule certain enemies untrippable (You can't trip a house, especially if you're standing in it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-24T20:23:20-08:00","id":1546364,"title":"","content":"I've noticed in a couple playthroughs that &quot;hold 2 curse dice&quot; seems to mean &quot;gain two curse dice and hold them until you bleed them off&quot;, but the written material, and other sources I've found through google searches, seem to suggest it means &quot;you have to be holding 2 curse dice to use this&quot;. Has it ever been officially confirmed which is correct? Even the official blog post seems a bit vague on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-24T21:02:26-08:00","id":1546366,"title":"","content":"Going by the text of chapter 4, all curse dice in your unspent pool are considered held. Effects that check your number of held curse dice simply require you to have that number of curse dice in your pool - for spells, you can activate them as long as you have at least that many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3388-r0gue_rob0t","name":"r0gue_rob0t","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-24T21:05:39-08:00","id":1546367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>r0gue_rob0t</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1546326-few-rules-questions?p=1546366#post1546366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going by the text of chapter 4, all curse dice in your unspent pool are considered held. Effects that check your number of held curse dice simply require you to have that number of curse dice in your pool - for spells, you can activate them as long as you have at least that many.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I thought as well, but I could have sworn I saw in the playthroughs on youtube that when a character cast a &quot;hold x curse dice&quot; spell they added those dice to their pool. Maybe I'm just going crazy and I'm not remembering the playthroughs properly.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-24T22:07:39-08:00","id":1546370,"title":"","content":"When picking contacts, do the contacts have to be of the same lineage/family/role as the character? Does an Outsider character have to pick an outsider as their lineage contact? Or does the contact just need to have access to the assets listed by the path?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T01:20:34-08:00","id":1546374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1546326-few-rules-questions?p=1546367#post1546367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what I thought as well, but I could have sworn I saw in the playthroughs on youtube that when a character cast a &quot;hold x curse dice&quot; spell they added those dice to their pool. Maybe I'm just going crazy and I'm not remembering the playthroughs properly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you don't <i>gain</i> curse dice when you're required to hold them. It's accounting for the curse dice you already hold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T01:21:04-08:00","id":1546375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1546326-few-rules-questions?p=1546370#post1546370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When picking contacts, do the contacts have to be of the same lineage/family/role as the character? Does an Outsider character have to pick an outsider as their lineage contact? Or does the contact just need to have access to the assets listed by the path?</div> </div> </div> </div>The contact doesn't even need to be Accursed. They just need the access listed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T03:53:49-08:00","id":1546376,"title":"","content":"Since you need a path skill to get favours from a contact I'm guessing you're not meant to have contacts outside your three paths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T04:38:27-08:00","id":1546377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1546326-few-rules-questions?p=1546367#post1546367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what I thought as well, but I could have sworn I saw in the playthroughs on youtube that when a character cast a &quot;hold x curse dice&quot; spell they added those dice to their pool. Maybe I'm just going crazy and I'm not remembering the playthroughs properly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is that the confusion comes from the two meanings of &quot;hold&quot; and &quot;pool&quot;.<br /> <br /> The number of CDs you have is the number of CDs you are &quot;holding&quot;, so your &quot;pool&quot; of CD is the number of CDs you &quot;hold&quot;.<br /> <br /> When you &quot;hold&quot; CD as part of a spell it just means that you need to have at least that number of CD in your pool.<br /> <br /> But *also* when you form a *dice* pool (your Skill + Attribute) you add your total &quot;held&quot; CD to that pool, so that might be what to were thinking (Also &quot;add&quot; is the wrong word really, you replace the dice one for one with curse dice, you don't roll extra dice).<br /> <br /> Finally you might just have seen an AP with misplays. I know Awkward GM Corbin did an early run through the Ashcan and that had a lot of errors in because they were new to the system. Also in the Ashcan there was language that suggested &quot;holding&quot; dice required you to roll them first, so that might have been the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T04:40:36-08:00","id":1546378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1546326-few-rules-questions?p=1546376#post1546376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since you need a path skill to get favours from a contact I'm guessing you're not meant to have contacts outside your three paths?</div> </div> </div> </div>Starting contacts *must* come from a Path (there's no other way to get them). It's a good shout as to whether contacts you buy later with XP have to be Path-linked too. It seems odd if they are but the system falls down a bit if they aren't.<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> To clarify, &quot;come from a Path&quot; means &quot;be mechanically derived from a path&quot;. If your Role Path is, say, Student then your Role Path Contacts are people you've met primarily through doing <i>student stuff</i>. That might be other students, it might be staff at your university, it might be a guy who comes into the coffee shop where you work part time to cover tuition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":". 11-25-2024, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}